From b2e367f727e8b0bb356127886d5de72808894085 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 11:17:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0079 -- OPL3 wub-wub fix part B: TL=0x3F all
 voices in SDL_DOSOpl3Shutdown

The OPL3 post-quit "wub-wub-wub" artifact (audible during play + persisting
post-quit per WAVE-46-LOG-ANALYSIS.md sec.0; H6 reg 0xBD chip-wide tremolo
hypothesis falsified at wave-47) was root-caused by sdl-engine + nx-engine
co-design on task #14 to two placeholder bank patches in MidiBackendOpl3.cpp
shipping RR=0 (release rate = 0 = infinite release time per YMF262 spec):
PATCH_ORGAN and PATCH_MALLET both have patch[3]/[9] bytes producing RR=0.
The smoking gun: PATCH_MALLET's comment says "very short release" but the
byte 0xC0 sets RR=0. Voices playing these patches never silence after
KEY-OFF -- the existing KEY-OFF triggers envelope RELEASE but RR=0 means
the release decays at rate 0 = never reaches silence -- so the chip
continues to emit audibly until power-down. The 3.7 Hz "wub-wub" cadence
is PATCH_ORGAN's FB=7 (max self-feedback) interacting with the chip's
hardware-fixed tremolo LFO clock through the stuck envelope.

The PRIMARY fix is engine-side: 4 bytes in MidiBackendOpl3.cpp's
PATCH_ORGAN and PATCH_MALLET to set RR=8. Companion engine patch ships
in the same iter.

This patch (SDL/0079) is the BELT-AND-BRACES SDL-side complement,
hardening the SDL_DOSOpl3Shutdown chip-state-teardown contract. The
existing contract ("silence all voices" + "restore OPL2 mode") is
INCOMPLETE: KEY-OFF only triggers envelope RELEASE -- it does not force
output silence. For any patch shipping RR=0 (the engine-side bug this
defends against, plus any future user-provided opl3-patches.dat loaded
via patch 0141 with the same authorship error), the existing contract
leaves the chip emitting. This patch adds a TL=0x3F (max attenuation,
-48 dB) sweep across both operators of all 18 voices BEFORE the KEY-OFF
loop. TL is the operator's amplitude attenuation per YMF262 spec; it
takes effect immediately on output, not gated by envelope phase. With
both ops at TL=0x3F across all 18 voices, the chip's audible output is
-48 dB == effectively silent regardless of envelope state / release
rate / chip-wide modulation.

Cost: 36 register writes * ~12 us per via the canonical Adlib inter-
write delay = ~432 us at chip-teardown only; no hot-path impact.
Default-ON; zero behavioral impact during play (existing NoteOff path
remains the in-play silence primitive; this only activates at chip-
teardown).

Per task #14 co-design 2026-05-26 + WAVE-46-LOG-ANALYSIS.md sec.6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c | 54 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 53 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c b/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
index f181de11f..066f78b2b 100644
--- a/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
+++ b/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
@@ -555,7 +555,59 @@ void SDL_DOSOpl3InitChip(void)
 
 void SDL_DOSOpl3Shutdown(void)
 {
-    /* Silence all voices first. */
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0079, OPL3 wub-wub fix part B):
+       zero TL (total level, reg 0x40+op) on both operators of all 18
+       voices to 0x3F (max attenuation, -48 dB) BEFORE the KEY-OFF-all
+       loop below. This forces the chip's audible output to silence
+       regardless of envelope state / release rate / any chip-wide
+       modulation -- belt-and-braces complement to the engine-side bank
+       fix (PATCH_ORGAN / PATCH_MALLET RR=0 -> RR=8 per task #14 wub-wub
+       co-design root-cause; companion engine patch in patches/nxengine-
+       evo/01NN). The engine fix is the primary mechanism; this SDL
+       sweep hardens the SDL_DOSOpl3Shutdown chip-state-teardown
+       contract so the existing "chip state safe for next process"
+       banner promise is literally true regardless of which patch bank
+       was loaded at runtime. Future-proofs against a user-provided
+       opl3-patches.dat (patch 0141 loader path) with the same RR=0
+       authorship bug.
+
+       Mechanism: KEY-OFF only triggers envelope RELEASE; the carrier
+       output then decays at the operator's RR (release rate). For
+       patches with RR=0 (the engine-side bug this defends against),
+       release time is INFINITE per YMF262 spec -- voices continue
+       emitting at near-pre-KEY-OFF level until power-down. TL=0x3F
+       takes effect immediately on the operator's output amplitude
+       (chip-spec-defined: TL is a direct attenuation, not envelope-
+       gated), so writing 0x3F silences the operator regardless of
+       envelope phase. With both operators of all 18 voices at TL=
+       0x3F, the chip's audible output is at -48 dB (effectively
+       inaudible).
+
+       Universally safe -- 0x3F is the OPL3 spec's max-attenuation
+       value, accepted on any compliant chip. Cost ~432 us at shutdown
+       (36 register writes * ~12 us each via SDL_DOSOpl3WriteRegister's
+       canonical inter-write delay); shutdown path, not on any hot
+       path. Default-ON, no killswitch -- zero behavioral impact during
+       play (the existing NoteOff path remains the in-play silence
+       primitive; this only activates at chip-teardown). Cross-link:
+       see task #14 co-design + WAVE-46-LOG-ANALYSIS.md sec.6. */
+    for (int v = 0; v < 18; v++) {
+        const uint16_t op0 = s_opl3_voice_offsets[v].op0_base;
+        const uint16_t op1 = s_opl3_voice_offsets[v].op1_base;
+        SDL_DOSOpl3WriteRegister((uint16_t)(0x40 + op0), 0x3F);
+        SDL_DOSOpl3WriteRegister((uint16_t)(0x40 + op1), 0x3F);
+    }
+    /* Two-witness banner for build-qa smoke per [[smoke_gate_discipline]]:
+       string in binary (".rodata" via this literal) + runtime emit in
+       <TAG>SDL.LOG when the shutdown path runs. */
+    doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0079 TL=0x3F sweep applied (18 voices "
+                     "x 2 ops, max attenuation -48 dB) on OPL3 chip-"
+                     "state teardown -- wub-wub fix part B engaged");
+
+    /* KEY-OFF all voices (clear bit 5 of 0xB0+ch; triggers envelope
+       release). After the TL=0x3F sweep above the audible output is
+       already silent; this returns the chip's per-voice KEY state to
+       "all off" for any next process. */
     for (int v = 0; v < 18; v++) {
         SDL_DOSOpl3VoiceNoteOff(v);
     }
